Thrilled to announce that I've finally achieved my goal of
ascending a character of every class with last night's Archeologist
ascension. I'm not sure why I've found Archeologist so challenging
(frankly, I had an easier time with Caveman), but an early
wish (Greyswandir) combined with finding a few of my own
former selves on bones levels - one with a spellbook of identify and
one with Magicbane -- managed to get my kit filled out fairly quickly. I
later found a magic lamp, got two wishes off thrones, and usual castle
wand, leaving me in the enviable position of entering the Astral Plane
with more than I needed (including, e.g., a helm of opposite alignment),
and a wish to spare, which went toward a blessed rubber chicken that
greatly sped up the endgame.

My only regret is that I was going for a vegetarian ascension,
but forgot that black puddings are non-veggie, and at one around the
time I was going to do the Quest. Alas. It was, however, a polyless and
polyselfless ascension.

